# A reply from the phone is typed into the session by CST, Enter and all. That must not
# leave a draft mark on the tab: the user's composer is empty, and the pencil said it
# was not. Seen live with the session attached and the cursor in its input box. Two
# tabs, because the strip with the markers is drawn only when there is more than one.

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_telegram private
session existing-app Existing app session
session other-app Other session

# Two tabs: whichever row is first opens first, then the other.
wait_for Other session
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Other session
press down
press enter
wait_for --resume=00000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000002

# A turn in the first tab, watched from the second so its end reaches the phone, which
# then has a message of that session's to reply to. Back to the first tab afterwards:
# cursor in the input box, nothing typed.
press ctrl+b p
wait_for --resume=00000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
type e2e:work 1500 Setup is done.
press enter
press ctrl+b n
telegram_wait Setup is done.
press ctrl+b p
wait_for --resume=00000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling

# The phone speaks to the session on screen. CST types it in and presses Enter; the
# stub never starts a turn on plain text, so nothing else could clear the slot.
telegram_say hello from the phone
wait_for Fake Copilot received: hello from the phone
telegram_wait reaction on
wait 1000
dump 01-no-phantom-draft
expect_not ✎

# Typing something now is a draft, as it always was.
type half a thought
wait 500
dump 02-real-draft
expect ✎
